its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nThe distance between the lines is $d=20\\,\\text{cm}=0.2\\,\\text{m}.$ Then, applying the parallel axis theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & =1.5+(0.2)^{2}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =1.5+0.2 \\\\  & =1.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia is $1.7\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-12bca215-1091-578b-aa86-b658265555c4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-12bca215-1091-578b-aa86-b658265555c4" :answer-field/id #uuid "12bca215-1091-578b-aa86-b658265555c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f059b9c9-6fc6-5a69-9ab0-e34a4c12e8f3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dcb61c04-31bf-503e-9b2e-5e242fc9850f" "answer-dc5659c0-08e0-5718-a418-64e181a7e44f" "answer-f059b9c9-6fc6-5a69-9ab0-e34a4c12e8f3" "answer-3179da0e-3638-5470-946e-1ba68d8e7a41" "answer-8b2581c2-d3fa-5830-911b-7de2d4f92b75"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dcb61c04-31bf-503e-9b2e-5e242fc9850f" :answer/id #uuid "dcb61c04-31bf-503e-9b2e-5e242fc9850f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.7\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dc5659c0-08e0-5718-a418-64e181a7e44f" :answer/id #uuid "dc5659c0-08e0-5718-a418-64e181a7e44f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.3\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f059b9c9-6fc6-5a69-9ab0-e34a4c12e8f3" :answer/id #uuid "f059b9c9-6fc6-5a69-9ab0-e34a4c12e8f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.7\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3179da0e-3638-5470-946e-1ba68d8e7a41" :answer/id #uuid "3179da0e-3638-5470-946e-1ba68d8e7a41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.1\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8b2581c2-d3fa-5830-911b-7de2d4f92b75" :answer/id #uuid "8b2581c2-d3fa-5830-911b-7de2d4f92b75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.5\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129546 :question/problem "Consider a plane lamina of mass $3\\,\\text{kg}$ and center of mass $(1,1),$ where $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters. If the moment of inertia of the lamina about an axis perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass is $1.5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2},$ what is the moment of inertia of the lamina about an axis parallel to the first passing through the point $(-3,4)?$" :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nThe distance between the line through the center of mass $(1,1)$ and the line through the point $(-3,4)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{(-3-1)^{2}+(4-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, applying the parallel axis theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & =1.5+{5}^{2}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =1.5+75 \\\\  & =76.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia is $76.5\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186126773 :answer-field/correct "answer-4cdc4a8e-a57f-57e0-bb50-35bd39671509" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a5f59f74-fc37-54c2-9b7b-14e1f15441b7" "answer-0878c284-4879-55be-912a-9656fbbc7c94" "answer-4cdc4a8e-a57f-57e0-bb50-35bd39671509" "answer-8a45685d-72c3-5e27-a219-4717f3dcc1b8" "answer-8a6a1caf-3346-52e6-8e61-695021764e2f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a5f59f74-fc37-54c2-9b7b-14e1f15441b7" :answer/id #uuid "a5f59f74-fc37-54c2-9b7b-14e1f15441b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "68.5\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0878c284-4879-55be-912a-9656fbbc7c94" :answer/id #uuid "0878c284-4879-55be-912a-9656fbbc7c94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "72.5\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4cdc4a8e-a57f-57e0-bb50-35bd39671509" :answer/id #uuid "4cdc4a8e-a57f-57e0-bb50-35bd39671509" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "76.5\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a45685d-72c3-5e27-a219-4717f3dcc1b8" :answer/id #uuid "8a45685d-72c3-5e27-a219-4717f3dcc1b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "82.5\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a6a1caf-3346-52e6-8e61-695021764e2f" :answer/id #uuid "8a6a1caf-3346-52e6-8e61-695021764e2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "88.5\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a98b9898-9990-5bdc-a565-d49f3ea3b73d" :question/id #uuid "a98b9898-9990-5bdc-a565-d49f3ea3b73d" :question/math-academy-id "q-164143" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $\\frac{9}{2}\\,\\text{kg}$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 4,\\,0\\le y\\le 4\\},$\nwhere $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters.\nFind the moment of inertia of the plate about a line perpendicular to $D$ at a distance of $2\\,\\text{m}$ from a parallel line passing through its center of mass." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=4\\cdot 4=16\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.$\nSince the plate has a uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{(\\frac{9}{2})}{16}=\\frac{9}{32}\\,\\text{kg}/{\\text{m}}^{2},\n$$\n\nand its center of mass is its centroid:\n\n$$\n(\\overset{¯}{x},\\overset{¯}{y})=(\\frac{0+4}{2},\\frac{0+4}{2})=(2,2)\n$$\n\nThen, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}((x-\\overset{¯}{x})^{2}+(y-\\overset{¯}{y})^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{32}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{4}9(x-2)^{2}+9(y-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{32}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{[9(x-2)^{2}y+3(y-2)^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{32}{\\int }_{0}^{4}36(x-2)^{2}+48\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{32}{[12(x-2)^{3}+48x]}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{32}(96+192-(-96)) \\\\  & =12\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line $2\\,\\text{m}$ from the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =12+{2}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & =12+18 \\\\  & =30\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ef625286-2a13-50df-81d4-0c23373fdb51"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ef625286-2a13-50df-81d4-0c23373fdb51" :answer-field/id #uuid "ef625286-2a13-50df-81d4-0c23373fdb51" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-82747faa-ed1e-5a88-b125-47a8d260239f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-59e32abc-46af-5bfb-8a64-d906d04f1614" "answer-b6ac6750-2ae1-5841-aad5-508161e918ee" "answer-95a1c2ed-0b14-59fe-afd7-b201b865e7d9" "answer-82747faa-ed1e-5a88-b125-47a8d260239f" "answer-a9aebf2a-4542-5040-a04e-0799607a819d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-59e32abc-46af-5bfb-8a64-d906d04f1614" :answer/id #uuid "59e32abc-46af-5bfb-8a64-d906d04f1614" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b6ac6750-2ae1-5841-aad5-508161e918ee" :answer/id #uuid "b6ac6750-2ae1-5841-aad5-508161e918ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95a1c2ed-0b14-59fe-afd7-b201b865e7d9" :answer/id #uuid "95a1c2ed-0b14-59fe-afd7-b201b865e7d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "28\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-82747faa-ed1e-5a88-b125-47a8d260239f" :answer/id #uuid "82747faa-ed1e-5a88-b125-47a8d260239f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a9aebf2a-4542-5040-a04e-0799607a819d" :answer/id #uuid "a9aebf2a-4542-5040-a04e-0799607a819d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "35\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-883c2bc8-ea50-58fe-851b-c16e2097cdb5" :question/id #uuid "883c2bc8-ea50-58fe-851b-c16e2097cdb5" :question/math-academy-id "q-164148" :question/problem "A rectangular plate occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 6\\}$\nand has mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{6}x,$ where $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters.\nGiven that the center of mass is at $(2,3),$ find the moment of inertia about a line perpendicular to $D$ at a distance of $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,\\text{m}$ from a parallel line passing through its center of mass." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nFirst, we find the mass of the plate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{6}\\frac{1}{6}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{6}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}{|}_{0}^{3}\\cdot y{|}_{0}^{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot \\frac{9}{2}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass $(2,3)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}((x-\\overset{¯}{x})^{2}+(y-\\overset{¯}{y})^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}((x-2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{6}((x-2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2})\\frac{x}{6}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{6}x(x-2)^{2}+x(y-3)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{[x(x-2)^{2}y+\\frac{1}{3}x(y-3)^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}6x(x-2)^{2}+18x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{3}6{x}^{3}-24{x}^{2}+42x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{[\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{4}-8{x}^{3}+21{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(\\frac{243}{2}-216+189-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot \\frac{189}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{63}{4}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,\\text{m}$ from the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =\\frac{63}{4}+{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{63}{4}+\\frac{9}{4} \\\\  & =18\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2d3c1b5c-5f38-591b-b4aa-e017dca1a997"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2d3c1b5c-5f38-591b-b4aa-e017dca1a997" :answer-field/id #uuid "2d3c1b5c-5f38-591b-b4aa-e017dca1a997" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2f7be1d0-d901-57d1-9262-308cd4b16cb7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-33730752-03eb-5584-b1de-cb94ac16c08b" "answer-2f7be1d0-d901-57d1-9262-308cd4b16cb7" "answer-85a7edbf-02fe-5b24-a716-394fd89efa4e" "answer-b2ce1d9b-5c76-570c-a685-19b16bac65bd" "answer-9a696841-434f-5e2a-ac85-3b84f6b2c204"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-33730752-03eb-5584-b1de-cb94ac16c08b" :answer/id #uuid "33730752-03eb-5584-b1de-cb94ac16c08b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2f7be1d0-d901-57d1-9262-308cd4b16cb7" :answer/id #uuid "2f7be1d0-d901-57d1-9262-308cd4b16cb7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-85a7edbf-02fe-5b24-a716-394fd89efa4e" :answer/id #uuid "85a7edbf-02fe-5b24-a716-394fd89efa4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{21}{2}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b2ce1d9b-5c76-570c-a685-19b16bac65bd" :answer/id #uuid "b2ce1d9b-5c76-570c-a685-19b16bac65bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{33}{4}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a696841-434f-5e2a-ac85-3b84f6b2c204" :answer/id #uuid "9a696841-434f-5e2a-ac85-3b84f6b2c204" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{45}{4}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9b0cf2d4-19bf-5bdf-8414-97d0c52886bd" :question/id #uuid "9b0cf2d4-19bf-5bdf-8414-97d0c52886bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-163817" :question/problem "Calculate the moment of inertia of a circular plate that occupies the region of a disk $D$ of radius $1\\,\\text{m}$ with mass density $\\lambda (x,y)={e}^{-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}},$ measured in $\\text{kg}/{\\text{m}}^{2},$ about a line perpendicular to the disk passing through a point on the circumference." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ can be expressed in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi \\}.\n$$\n\nSince the mass density is symmetric in $x$ and $y,$ its center of mass is at $(0,0).$ The mass density function, in polar coordinates, is given by $\\lambda (r,\\theta )={e}^{-{r}^{2}}.$\n\nNext, we find the mass of the plate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{-{r}^{2}}\\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}r{e}^{-{r}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}r\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-{r}^{2}}{|}_{0}^{1}\\cdot \\theta {|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\frac{1}{e})\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =\\pi (1-\\frac{1}{e})\\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{-{r}^{2}}\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{r}^{3}{e}^{-{r}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}r\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}({r}^{2}+1){e}^{-{r}^{2}}{|}_{0}^{1}\\cdot \\theta {|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{e})\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =\\pi (1-\\frac{2}{e})\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line passing through a point on the circumference is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =\\pi (1-\\frac{2}{e})+{1}^{2}\\cdot \\pi (1-\\frac{1}{e}) \\\\  & =\\pi (1-\\frac{2}{e}+1-\\frac{1}{e}) \\\\  & =\\pi (2-\\frac{3}{e})\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-759b288f-9c42-51b4-b2fb-e9f142c0ea9a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-759b288f-9c42-51b4-b2fb-e9f142c0ea9a" :answer-field/id #uuid "759b288f-9c42-51b4-b2fb-e9f142c0ea9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-913539ca-2d7a-54d5-b8ee-0ae5cbab6a86" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0a863b7c-edfd-5ed3-b733-c20e15e56c23" "answer-e13ceabb-d833-566f-a6f9-760558e61eeb" "answer-56e8f7cf-5f92-5e36-9bcd-9ee37ee18eb7" "answer-913539ca-2d7a-54d5-b8ee-0ae5cbab6a86" "answer-874f21f4-6ea1-564f-aaae-2fe439042176"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0a863b7c-edfd-5ed3-b733-c20e15e56c23" :answer/id #uuid "0a863b7c-edfd-5ed3-b733-c20e15e56c23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi }{3e}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e13ceabb-d833-566f-a6f9-760558e61eeb" :answer/id #uuid "e13ceabb-d833-566f-a6f9-760558e61eeb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6e}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-56e8f7cf-5f92-5e36-9bcd-9ee37ee18eb7" :answer/id #uuid "56e8f7cf-5f92-5e36-9bcd-9ee37ee18eb7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi (1-\\frac{2}{e})\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-913539ca-2d7a-54d5-b8ee-0ae5cbab6a86" :answer/id #uuid "913539ca-2d7a-54d5-b8ee-0ae5cbab6a86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi (2-\\frac{3}{e})\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-874f21f4-6ea1-564f-aaae-2fe439042176" :answer/id #uuid "874f21f4-6ea1-564f-aaae-2fe439042176" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi (3-\\frac{5}{e})\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7f698f1e-e965-5c52-9d4f-e9787cc01568" :question/id #uuid "7f698f1e-e965-5c52-9d4f-e9787cc01568" :question/math-academy-id "q-163814" :question/problem "A circular plate of mass $4\\,\\text{kg}$ and uniform mass density occupies the region of a disk $D$ of radius $1\\,\\text{m}$ centered at the origin.\nFind the moment of inertia of the plate about a line perpendicular to $D$ at a distance of $2\\,\\text{m}$ from a parallel line passing through its center of mass." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ can be expressed in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 1,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi \\}.\n$$\n\nThe area of the circular plate $D$ is $A=\\pi \\cdot {1}^{2}=\\pi \\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.$\nSince the plate has a uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{4}{\\pi }\\,\\text{kg}/{\\text{m}}^{2},\n$$\n\nand its center of mass is its centroid $(0,0).$\n\nThen, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}{r}^{4}{|}_{0}^{1}\\cdot \\theta {|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =2\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line $2\\,\\text{m}$ from the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =2+{2}^{2}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =2+16 \\\\  & =18\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8eb70cd3-bd0e-53c1-a34c-a4e5cb97073f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8eb70cd3-bd0e-53c1-a34c-a4e5cb97073f" :answer-field/id #uuid "8eb70cd3-bd0e-53c1-a34c-a4e5cb97073f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-82451b16-4f7c-56b9-8377-2102d860c661" :answer-field/choices ["answer-764d4bb7-3ff1-5f4b-acc9-78c80102bfee" "answer-82451b16-4f7c-56b9-8377-2102d860c661" "answer-d6536ccb-e3d4-55c3-b971-e406d90e2407" "answer-d996a8d9-ac23-5775-b502-1c0e09b1c5d6" "answer-a0529374-1496-5e12-843a-0505f36865b2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-764d4bb7-3ff1-5f4b-acc9-78c80102bfee" :answer/id #uuid "764d4bb7-3ff1-5f4b-acc9-78c80102bfee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-82451b16-4f7c-56b9-8377-2102d860c661" :answer/id #uuid "82451b16-4f7c-56b9-8377-2102d860c661" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d6536ccb-e3d4-55c3-b971-e406d90e2407" :answer/id #uuid "d6536ccb-e3d4-55c3-b971-e406d90e2407" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d996a8d9-ac23-5775-b502-1c0e09b1c5d6" :answer/id #uuid "d996a8d9-ac23-5775-b502-1c0e09b1c5d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a0529374-1496-5e12-843a-0505f36865b2" :answer/id #uuid "a0529374-1496-5e12-843a-0505f36865b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129550 :question/problem "A circular plate of mass $6\\,\\text{kg}$ with uniform mass density occupies the region of a disk $D$ of radius $3\\,\\text{m}$ and is centered at the origin.\nGiven that the moment of inertia of the plate about a line $l$ perpendicular to the plate is $39\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2},$ find the distance of the line $l$ from the center of mass of $D.$" :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ can be expressed in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 3,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi \\}.\n$$\n\nThe area of the circular plate $D$ is $A=\\pi \\cdot {3}^{2}=9\\pi \\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.$\nSince the plate has a uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{6}{9\\pi }=\\frac{2}{3\\pi }\\,\\text{kg}/{\\text{m}}^{2},\n$$\n\nand its center of mass is its centroid $(0,0).$\n\nThen, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}{r}^{4}{|}_{0}^{3}\\cdot \\theta {|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{81}{4}\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =27\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem and solving for $d,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\ 39 & =27+6{d}^{2} \\\\ 6{d}^{2} & =12 \\\\ {d}^{2} & =2 \\\\ d & =\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186126797 :answer-field/correct "answer-8e2eecdc-200a-5731-8433-4d7de3a0d3fb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8ec20448-d6e9-5faa-8568-2a10c85abae3" "answer-0993c715-5235-5e81-99f8-e0df49df41fd" "answer-13c67ee2-4b4a-554c-addc-8d24167bac80" "answer-8e2eecdc-200a-5731-8433-4d7de3a0d3fb" "answer-217da9bf-7efe-5f53-aedd-b0bd54330075"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ec20448-d6e9-5faa-8568-2a10c85abae3" :answer/id #uuid "8ec20448-d6e9-5faa-8568-2a10c85abae3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0993c715-5235-5e81-99f8-e0df49df41fd" :answer/id #uuid "0993c715-5235-5e81-99f8-e0df49df41fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-13c67ee2-4b4a-554c-addc-8d24167bac80" :answer/id #uuid "13c67ee2-4b4a-554c-addc-8d24167bac80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e2eecdc-200a-5731-8433-4d7de3a0d3fb" :answer/id #uuid "8e2eecdc-200a-5731-8433-4d7de3a0d3fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-217da9bf-7efe-5f53-aedd-b0bd54330075" :answer/id #uuid "217da9bf-7efe-5f53-aedd-b0bd54330075" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0d33e1be-cff3-50e5-94dd-6992342f9938" :question/id #uuid "0d33e1be-cff3-50e5-94dd-6992342f9938" :question/math-academy-id "q-164146" :question/problem "A rectangular plate occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 6\\}$\nand has mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{1}{12}y,$ where $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters. The moment of inertia of the plate about a line $l$ perpendicular to the plate is $\\frac{31}{4}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.$\nGiven that the center of mass of the plate is at $(1,4),$ find the distance of the line $l$ from the center of mass." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nFirst, we find the mass of the plate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{6}\\frac{1}{12}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{6}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\cdot x\\,{|}_{0}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\cdot 2\\cdot 18 \\\\  & =3\\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass $(1,4)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}((x-\\overset{―}{x})^{2}+(y-\\overset{―}{y})^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}((x-1)^{2}+(y-4)^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{6}((x-1)^{2}+(y-4)^{2})\\cdot \\frac{1}{12}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{6}(x-1)^{2}y+{y}^{3}-8{y}^{2}+16y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{2}(x-1)^{2}{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{4}-\\frac{8}{3}{y}^{3}+8{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{\\int }_{0}^{2}18(x-1)^{2}+324-576+288\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{\\int }_{0}^{2}18{x}^{2}-36x+54\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{[6{x}^{3}-18{x}^{2}+54x]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}(48-72+108) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\cdot 84 \\\\  & =7\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem and solving for $d,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\ \\frac{31}{4} & =7+3{d}^{2} \\\\ 3{d}^{2} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ {d}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ d & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-31d9aa89-1ce2-5fa3-ba0a-15ff00f5c864"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-31d9aa89-1ce2-5fa3-ba0a-15ff00f5c864" :answer-field/id #uuid "31d9aa89-1ce2-5fa3-ba0a-15ff00f5c864" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e025c665-16ab-588f-8312-dd91f1944aed" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c751f541-41e0-5201-93fb-107f49f6b75a" "answer-e025c665-16ab-588f-8312-dd91f1944aed" "answer-b78b6c21-f632-5a26-b72d-a537bfece296" "answer-ee9e8082-d12a-577b-aaf0-a262ae52759f" "answer-47e8cfaf-fd1b-55f7-8116-1f0008be7b3d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c751f541-41e0-5201-93fb-107f49f6b75a" :answer/id #uuid "c751f541-41e0-5201-93fb-107f49f6b75a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e025c665-16ab-588f-8312-dd91f1944aed" :answer/id #uuid "e025c665-16ab-588f-8312-dd91f1944aed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b78b6c21-f632-5a26-b72d-a537bfece296" :answer/id #uuid "b78b6c21-f632-5a26-b72d-a537bfece296" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee9e8082-d12a-577b-aaf0-a262ae52759f" :answer/id #uuid "ee9e8082-d12a-577b-aaf0-a262ae52759f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-47e8cfaf-fd1b-55f7-8116-1f0008be7b3d" :answer/id #uuid "47e8cfaf-fd1b-55f7-8116-1f0008be7b3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186130459 :tutorial/content "Consider a plane lamina that occupies the region $D \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}^2$ of mass $M$ where the center of mass is at $\\left(\\bar{x},\\bar{y}\\right).$\n\n![](images/4c/4c2c7e3525dfe8aea3cce69a7332ccf5ca82ddfe37657071ddef35650bcea383.png)\n\nWe know that the lamina has some moment of inertia $I_M$ about the line $l_M$ that passes through the center of mass and is perpendicular to the lamina.\n\n![](images/96/9638e9d47ef3c9b2fab47f39cf70e2ba07863c6e949755c8378e5737caa0a350.png)\n\nNow, if $l$ is a line parallel to $l_M,$ then the lamina also has moment of inertia about $l,$ say $I_l.$\n\n![](images/06/06819ca45bd176ff9d36b07c73574bc9f2911a7b0b96b5b916ba76f8606d2f60.png)\n\nGiven the value of $I_M,$ we can find $I_l$ using the **parallel axis theorem**, which states that\n\n$$\nI_l = I_M + d^2M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines.\n\nThe term $d^2M$ is the moment of inertia about $l$ of the lamina when its entire mass is concentrated at the center of mass.\n\n![](images/fb/fbab9fab43dd45fd80008704f406f94864cac57d636320d250dca86ff465f196.png)\n\nSo, our interpretation of the parallel axis theorem is the following:\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\text{moment of inertia of }D \\ \\text{about a parallel line }l}_{I_l}\n\\:=\\:\n\\underbrace{\\text{moment of inertia of }D \\ \\text{about the center of mass}}_{I_M}\n\\:+\\:\n\\underbrace{\\text{moment of inertia of point mass }M \\ \\text{about the parallel line } l}_{d^2M}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $d^2M$ is always positive, we have $I_M \\leq I_l$ for any line $l$ perpendicular to the lamina. In other words, the moment of inertia about the line through its center of mass is the *smallest* moment of inertia about any line in that direction." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129370 :activity/expected-seconds 1440.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
